rav1r

rav1r derives from rav1e (https://github.com/xiph/rav1e). The base is the
master branch at commit 31435de9d76fddd38f6dcc31d4014574cebb2092.

rav1e is copyright the rav1e contributors, including Thomas Daede and the
other authors in the upstream git history at
https://github.com/xiph/rav1e/graphs/contributors. Copyright notices in the
files and in LICENSE keep their original wording.

LICENSE holds the BSD 2-Clause License. PATENTS holds the Alliance for Open
Media Patent License 1.0. Both apply to rav1r and stay unchanged.

Files with their own headers keep them in place:

- The assembly under src/x86 and src/arm names VideoLAN and the dav1d
  authors, Two Orioles, LLC, Martin Storsjo, Janne Grunau, VideoLabs,
  Matthias Dressel, B Krishnan Iyer, and Nathan Egge.
- src/ext/x86/x86inc.asm names the x264 project and its authors.

Source and binary distributions of rav1r reproduce LICENSE, PATENTS, and this
notice, as those files require.

Code inlined from other crates keeps its notice at the head of each file.

